      "side": 1,
      "message": "“vci-pos” is the VCI bit position in VCI registers, e.g. IE[6:1] in VCI INPUT ENABLE REGISTER, bit1 is for VCI_IN1 and bit2 is for VCI_IN2…, it doesn’t fix to a specific GPIO.\nNot sure if I capture your question.\n\nActually, you may bring up one concern which we are aware in developing,\"gpios:\" property is not really used in this VCI logic, it can be removed optionally.",
